<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Batista flees Cuba as Castro's revolution triumphs</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Dictator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fulgencio-batista">Fulgencio Batista</a> fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/havana">Havana</a> in the early hours, handing victory to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fidel-castro">Fidel Castro</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrillas</a>. The new revolutionary government later aligned with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, reshaping the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cold-war">Cold War</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union launches Luna 1 towards the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Luna 1 lifted off from Baikonur and became the first spacecraft to reach escape velocity. It missed the Moon but passed close by and entered orbit around the Sun, the first human-made object to do so.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-3">3 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Alaska becomes the 49th US state</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> signed the proclamation admitting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a> to the Union. Purchased from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1867, it became the largest state by area, more than twice the size of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaska">Alaska</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-4">4 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Luna 1 becomes the first spacecraft to pass the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet probe flew within about 6,000 km of the Moon's surface before heading into orbit around the Sun. Its instruments made the first direct measurements of the solar wind.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-8">8 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Charles de Gaulle takes office as President of France</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> became the first President of the Fifth Republic, whose constitution greatly strengthened the executive. He governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until 1969, ending the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> in 1962.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-3">3 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Buddy Holly, Ritchie Valens and the Big Bopper die in a plane crash</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Their light aircraft crashed in snow near Clear Lake, Iowa, shortly after take-off, killing all aboard. Don McLean later called it 'the day the music died' in his song 'American Pie'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valens">Valens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-9">9 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Soviet R-7 becomes the first operational ICBM</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The R-7 Semyorka, the rocket that had launched Sputnik, entered service as the world's first intercontinental ballistic missile. Its descendants still launch Soyuz spacecraft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-21">21 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Hawaii becomes the 50th US state</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dwight-d-eisenhower">Eisenhower</a> proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a>'s admission as the 50th state. It was the first state outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a> and the first with an Asian American plurality.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-7">7 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Luna 3 photographs the far side of the Moon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet probe Luna 3 took the first photographs of the Moon's far side, which is never visible from Earth. The grainy images revealed a surface with far fewer dark lunar 'seas' than the near side.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-1">1 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Twelve nations sign the Antarctic Treaty</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">In Washington, twelve countries, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, agreed to reserve Antarctica for peaceful scientific research. The treaty banned military activity and froze territorial claims.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hawaii-admission-act">Hawaii Admission Act</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Hawaii Admission Act was a law of the United States Congress signed by President Dwight D. Eisenhower on 18 March 1959.</p></div></li></ol></section>
